Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.40,0:00:03.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Every morning, before the city woke,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.94,0:00:08.57,Default,,0,0,0,,my grandmother spread\Nfresh grass on the floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.57,0:00:17.56,Default,,0,0,0,,She washed the green beans slowly.\NShe never rushed coffee.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.56,0:00:26.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Then came the fire, and the smell\Nthat called the neighbours in.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.01,0:00:34.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Incense filled the room.\NIt was her way of saying: welcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.37,0:00:40.40,Default,,0,0,0,,The sound of grinding was\Nthe first music of my day.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.40,0:00:48.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Then we waited. She taught me\Nthat waiting is part of the gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.37,0:00:54.81,Default,,0,0,0,,One pot. Many cups.\NNo one was ever left out.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.37,0:01:04.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Three rounds: abol, tona,\Nand baraka, the blessing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.53,0:01:09.49,Default,,0,0,0,,By the third cup,\Nstrangers had become family.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.53,0:01:17.55,Default,,0,0,0,,'Stay a little longer,' she always\Nsaid. 'The coffee is still warm.'
